Fix TATE rotation direction on GLCore with GLSL shaders (issue #18488)

gl3_set_rotation() uses 270 * rotation for everything except hardware
rendered cores with a bottom-left origin. That direction is meant for the
Slang path, where the filter chain applies the rotation itself.

The GLSL (.glslp) render chain of the gl3 driver follows the gl2
conventions instead: the frame is drawn with flipped vertex positions
(chain.vertex_ptr = gl3_vertexes_flipped) and rotated by gl->mvp, exactly
like gl2, which always uses 90 * rotation. With 270 * rotation the result
is off by 180 degrees, so TATE games were displayed upside down as soon as
a GLSL preset was loaded (the overlay stayed correct, since overlays are
always drawn with mvp_no_rot).

Use the gl2 rotation direction when the GLSL chain is active, and recompute
the rotation in gl3_set_shader(), since switching presets at runtime can
toggle chain.active without going through a driver reinit.

--- a/gfx/drivers/gl3.c
+++ b/gfx/drivers/gl3.c
@@ -3345,6 +3345,8 @@
    return false;
 }
 
+static void gl3_set_rotation(void *data, unsigned rotation);
+
 static bool gl3_set_shader(void *data,
       enum rarch_shader_type type, const char *path)
 {
@@ -3384,6 +3386,10 @@
    if (!gl3_init_filter_chain_with_path(gl, path))
       return false;
 
+   /* chain.active may have just changed, and the rotation direction depends
+    * on it, so recompute it for the new chain. */
+   gl3_set_rotation(gl, retroarch_get_rotation());
+
    if (gl->flags & GL3_FLAG_USE_SHARED_CONTEXT)
       gl->ctx_driver->bind_hw_render(gl->ctx_data, true);
 
@@ -3397,7 +3403,11 @@
    if (!gl)
       return;
 
-   if (video_driver_is_hw_context() && (gl->flags & GL3_FLAG_HW_RENDER_BOTTOM_LEFT))
+   /* The GLSL render chain uses the gl2 conventions (flipped vertex positions
+    * plus gl->mvp), so it needs the gl2 rotation direction. The 270 case is
+    * for the Slang path, whose filter chain handles rotation itself. */
+   if (     gl->chain.active
+         || (video_driver_is_hw_context() && (gl->flags & GL3_FLAG_HW_RENDER_BOTTOM_LEFT)))
       gl->rotation = 90 * rotation;
    else
       gl->rotation = 270 * rotation;
